DISCLAIMER — MEDICAL ADMINISTRATIVE SOFTWARE

This software is provided for administrative and record-keeping purposes within
a dental clinic context only.

  1. NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE
     This software is not a certified medical device and has not been evaluated
     or approved by any medical regulatory body. It does not provide clinical
     diagnoses, treatment recommendations, drug prescriptions, or medical advice
     of any kind. X-ray images stored in the system are administrative records
     only; their clinical interpretation is the sole responsibility of licensed
     medical professionals.

  2. REGULATORY COMPLIANCE
     Operators are solely responsible for compliance with all applicable laws
     and regulations in their jurisdiction, including but not limited to:
     — Palestinian Personal Data Protection Law and related regulations
     — Palestinian Monetary Authority (PMA) regulations for electronic payment
       acceptance and merchant licensing
     — PCI-DSS standards if processing real cardholder data
     — Any applicable international standards (HIPAA, GDPR) where the operator
       has obligations under those frameworks
     — Palestinian medical records retention and destruction requirements

  3. PAYMENT GATEWAY DISCLAIMER
     The four payment gateways included (Bank of Palestine, Jawwal Pay, PalPay,
     PayPal) are implemented as sandbox simulators for development and
     demonstration purposes. Processing real patient payments requires:
     (a) Obtaining live credentials from each gateway provider
     (b) Completing the provider's merchant onboarding and compliance review
     (c) Implementing real webhook signature verification in the callback route
     (d) PCI-DSS compliance assessment appropriate to the integration scope
     The authors make no warranty that the current integration patterns meet
     any gateway provider's production requirements.

  4. CURRENCY CONVERSION
     The ILS-to-USD exchange rate used for PayPal transactions is a static,
     manually configured value. The authors make no warranty as to its accuracy
     and accept no liability for financial discrepancies arising from rate drift.
     Operators must implement live FX rate retrieval before accepting real PayPal
     payments from patients.

  5. DATA SECURITY
     Operators are responsible for securing their deployment environment,
     including: HTTPS enforcement, firewall rules, database access controls,
     secret rotation, backup and disaster recovery, and log management.
     Sensitive patient files (national ID scans, X-ray images) are stored on
     a non-web-accessible disk by default; operators must not alter this
     configuration in a way that exposes these files publicly.

  6. NO WARRANTY ON CLINICAL DATA INTEGRITY
     The system stores what medical professionals enter. It does not validate
     the clinical accuracy, completeness, or appropriateness of diagnoses,
     treatment notes, tooth numbers, condition types, or any other clinical
     record entered by users.

